        "original_id": "2307e2b1-bae0-504b-8caa-4265ec368c1b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Collins, Blackie Lawless, Jack Lee, Peter Case, Nikki Sixx\n- Bands: The Nerves, Sister, W.A.S.P., New York Dolls, Mötley Crüe\n- Places: New York City, Los Angeles\n- Roles: writer, author, music producer, multi-instrumentalist, songwriter, lead singer, rhythm guitarist, bassist, drummer, guitarist\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Vincent Collins was born in 1956 in New York City and is an American writer, author, music producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Blackie Lawless was born as Steven Edward Duren on September 4, 1956, and is an American songwriter and musician.\n- The Nerves were a mid-1970s American power pop trio based in Los Angeles featuring guitarist Jack Lee, bassist Peter Case, and drummer Paul Collins.\n- Blackie Lawless was formerly a member of the New York Dolls and later became the lead singer and rhythm guitarist, and formerly bassist, for W.A.S.P.\n- Former members of Sister included Blackie Lawless and Nikki Sixx, and Nikki Sixx later co-created Mötley Crüe.",
